runtime changes: 0.4.31 → 0.4.33
## 0.4.33

- Declare independent security invariants beside access rules. `check` reports proved, refuted with a replayable counterexample, or unproved. Supported local rule implications, typed aggregate contributor audiences and exact server lifetime admission have scoped proofs; general temporal histories, opaque writers, capture/live-parent reductions and disconnected-device freshness remain explicitly unproved. Passing finite challenges is not a universal security proof.
- `audit` (also `check --audit`, with JSON output) lists conditional role/row/column/effect exposure and grant writers, including uncovered paths. Bakeoff advice flags grants outliving roles, argument-driven grants, missing evidence, sweep-only deadlines and existence oracles; non-whitespace text minima apply consistently on server and device.
- `test` runs generated adversarial engine histories and real HTTP unsigned, forged and revoked-session attempts by default, including declared seats and bounded argument/media combinations. Upgraded apps receive campaigns without adding files; declared-policy violations fail. Apps without invariants get one aggregate missing-intent note, not a refusal, and an ignored reviewable `snapback/generated/security-invariants.q.draft` that is never compiled or accepted automatically. Add product-specific invariants and business cases; zero business cases still require explicit `--fixture-only`.
- `deploy --staging` classifies only a fresh store. `guide staging` provisions real password users and first admin with ordinary signup plus an operator-authorized application mutation; production/legacy stores cannot be relabelled. `startServe` exposes `operatorToken()`, `seedAccounts()` and `seedUsers`/`sessions`; bulk setup refuses production before minting credentials or creating accounts.
- Password-only apps close persona headers, `/seed` and `/dev/*` by default even under `dev`. Fixture workflows explicitly request `--unsafe-dev-doors` and declared personas. `startDev` persists by default; use `args:["--memory"]` for disposable tests. Adapt recognizes shipped older proofs while preserving custom scripts.
- React/Expo `useQueryData` returns data or undefined and throws typed `QueryRefusal`; `useQueryResult` offers inline refusal and precise read evidence. Partial/stale data remains displayable; use `useQuery`/`usePage` for completeness, freshness and pagination. `SignedIn` follows the app auth snapshot; `useAppReady` retains initial restoration across releases.
- Starters stop copying unused production recipes into apps; runnable slices remain in installed guide assets. Completeness notes lead with checked query rewrites and preserve distinct same-site findings and source-bound acknowledgement. `hourOfDay(t)` is UTC 0..23; `hour(t)` remains epoch hours. Money arguments use integer minor units without implicit rounding; sweep advice names row deadlines and leaves opening/closing/equality policy explicit.

## 0.4.32

- Existing stores retain rows, ids and captured `read through` authority. Upgrading alone does not convert copy-column recipes or expand audiences. To use `read through live .parent`, declare a required immutable reference and per-parent product cap, regenerate declarations and rebuild web/native/Exact engines for `live-parent-copy-v1`. Adoption validates manual copies against current parents and refuses inconsistent copies atomically; repair them explicitly first. Live-to-manual rollback reconciles current audience cells, including dormant ones, rather than restoring stale grants.
- Live-parent authority follows the complete current parent rule. Parent writes prepay maximum fanout, maintain private child copies and invalidate/sync moves atomically; devices queue parent writes. Exact single-audience sync is all-current; other whole parent rules remain online. Time, chained live inheritance, derived/receipt/action/index compositions outside the first form refuse. Bulk loads require coherent bounded batches. `guide rule-recipes current-roster` includes live and manual forms; three-level shared authority flattens one ordinary root onto independent direct live children.
- Clock advances coalesce arbitrarily many crossed windows; the 10,000-window cap applies only to `--each-boundary`. Replies retain exact skipped counts, up to 32 replay commands per schedule and omitted counts. Replay commands carry the live dev port; reasons list every admitted window through slow maintenance, offsets stay exact and skew/now share a sample. `waitForClock` observes the registered page client's advanced clock.
- Production entry restores persisted account/device custody before background `/auth/config` discovery, including offline with no discovery cache. Principal scans skip hidden/test/acceptance/fixture/proof sources while retaining runtime scripts. Production adaptation proposes explicit service-seat provisioning for writer-less enum-role rosters and points persona-only upgrades to `init --adapt --production`; existing application writers and screens remain owned. Guests-only identity and guest-to-account isolation are explicit.
- `useAppReady()` records successful initial restoration for the mounted app/viewer and stays true across release switches and later admission warnings. Account/app/restoration boundaries reset it. Keep drafts above release/role branches; protected actions still need current complete, fresh, non-revalidating role evidence and operation availability. SDK/server admission remains authoritative. Generated evolved fields explain missing-release optionality; conditional enum projections retain literal/nullable unions. Device-less identity errors name `sessionStore`; complete empty lists remain `absent`, and file uploads use `{file:{…}}`.
- Review static compiler notes explicitly with `check --ack-notes`. Shareable `snapback/check-notes.json` invalidates on any Quarry source/module edit or changed finding. Text prints new notes; verbose/JSON retain all findings, with `newNotes` and `acknowledgedNotes` partitioning `notes`, including failed checks. Dynamic store/readiness findings cannot be acknowledged. Malformed acknowledgement files refuse without overwrite.
- Quarry preserves declared cursors through planner fallback, recognizes mandatory later atomic lookups and key-equal computed locals, and accepts typed literal `in [...]` maintained predicates. Probe notes name backing unique keys; sync-order notes distinguish ordinary server reads from held offline data. `N_REQUIRE_REFUSED` checks human branches independently of service alternatives; new `N_QUERY_FILTERED` identifies returned branches missing read-rule proof. `E_QUARRY_DUPLICATE_RULE` has dedicated recovery; shape joins name incompatible row tables. Cascade advice names enabling delete rules and keeps arithmetic in verbose/JSON/why; atomic fanout advice offers product caps or jobs. `guide cleanup` executes cleanup and active-row/history patterns; no checked-reference annotation is introduced.
- Authorization recipes execute hidden reads before business requires, hidden unique-conflict suppression and rule-versus-program `exists`; readable totals, presence-gated durable handoffs with disconnect grace, scheduled publication/withdrawal/reapproval, private booking counts, opted-in leaderboards and versioned private history are compiled and packed-tested. These recipes preserve each application's explicit disclosure policy.
- Starter advice distinguishes recognized older native helpers from sign-in-mode changes and preserves edited helpers. Empty saved versions mean “not saved yet”; malformed nonempty snapshots still refuse. Adapt previews every package/file edit and day-two marker, reports all-module flat/saved differences, and removes only recognized todo leftovers from custom-schema Home starters. Placeholder/snapshot advice uses exact shipped digests; custom proof advice is labeled heuristic.
- `test` refuses zero executed business cases unless `--fixture-only` is explicit; `testSource` forwards `{fixtureOnly:true}`. `deploy --save-version versions/vN` captures selected modules, contemporary fixtures and the actual immutable release label without replacing evidence. `upgrade --quiet` keeps per-project actions and both failure streams. Release previews group related facts and lead rollback with lost guards/refusal codes; internal index paths require verbose/JSON. Restoration conflicts identify actual duplicate groups. `rollback --check --bridge <new-dir>` writes current source and an app-specific operator checklist without activation.
- Release consumers refuse missing/release-less deployments before creating files; deploy creates deployments. Persisted database selection wins over stale/missing convenience pointers, while administrative inspection remains available with damaged retained source. New dev-only `seed` loads fixtures through an identified running host. Release JSON adds `current` equal to `release`, and its `current` source selector differs from latest after rollback. Help/parser coverage includes all new flags. Long guide previews keep the opening, first section and index without partial code fences; use `--full`. `bootstrap` opens production guidance, deploy help names source/deployment paths, and init's port note requires an environment range.
- Proof mismatches name argument keys; full armed/actual values go only to a private mode-0600 witness log whose failures cannot block writes. Substring advice requires explicit matching scope; timeouts name visible headings. Fixtures validate URLs and identify refused personas/token fingerprints without bearer bytes. Missing static output names the app's build script; browser helpers check their peer first. Dev-reset online clients halt with `E_DEV_RESET`, retaining unknown write outcomes and no automatic retries. Fixture aliases traverse zero-based arrays; test output explains its columns and explicit `--as` precedence. Testing includes a complete production-account day-two proof and generated proof API table; wire guidance starts with executable literal envelopes.
